        <mxCell id="c77" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined in coral: the Plant row, whose use of practical capacity falls from 71.6% to 54.4% when FUR-BNH, FUR-NGT, FUR-TBL are bought. Outlined in teal: Quality Assurance, which frees nothing, because none of the three families is routed through it. The formula bar shows the first freed cell, a SUMPRODUCT over the Activity Table weighted by whether the family is bought; the use columns divide by the practical capacity of column E.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="343" width="860" height="53" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
